---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base>
  <!-- ─── Hero ─── -->
  <div class="site-container">
    <header class="hero">
      <div class="hero__status">
        <span class="hero__status-dot"></span>
        Building production AI systems
      </div>
      <div class="hero__name">Dr. Nan Shang</div>
      <div class="hero__title">Chief Scientist & Founding Engineer</div>
      <div class="hero__org">Drone Institute</div>
      <p class="hero__summary">
        Geospatial AI systems architect. Building production-grade,
        constraint-aware systems that transform complex spatial data into
        reliable operational outcomes.
      </p>
      <div class="hero__links">
        <a class="hero__link" href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=TcDAyj0AAAAJ&hl=en"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Scholar</a>
        <a class="hero__link" href="https://github.com/leibowivz"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        <a class="hero__link" href="mailto:nan.shang@droneinstitute.ai">Contact</a>
      </div>
    </header>
  </div>

  <!-- ─── Navigation ─── -->
  <nav class="nav" aria-label="Primary">
    <div class="nav__inner">
      <a class="nav__link" href="#overview">Overview</a>
      <a class="nav__link" href="#philosophy">Philosophy</a>
      <a class="nav__link" href="#systems">Systems</a>
      <a class="nav__link" href="#research">Research</a>
      <a class="nav__link" href="#engineering">Engineering</a>
      <a class="nav__link" href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <main class="site-container">

    <!-- ─── Overview ─── -->
    <section id="overview">
      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>
        Work spans remote sensing research, large-scale geospatial pipelines,
        and AI systems engineering — with an emphasis on translating academic
        methods into deployable, auditable, and maintainable infrastructure.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">
        Rather than optimizing isolated model performance, the focus is on
        system behavior under real-world constraints: runtime, cost envelopes,
        data drift, verification, and long-term iteration.
      </p>

      <div class="responsibilities">
        <div class="kv-item__key">Responsibilities</div>
        <ul class="subsection__list">
          <li>Defining technical direction grounded in research rigor</li>
          <li>Architecting end-to-end geospatial and AI systems</li>
          <li>Owning system-level trade-offs across accuracy, performance, cost, and reliability</li>
          <li>Bridging research outputs with production deployment</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── Philosophy ─── -->
    <section id="philosophy">
      <h2>Philosophy</h2>

      <div class="philosophy-grid">
        <div class="philosophy-card">
          <div class="philosophy-card__num">01</div>
          <div class="philosophy-card__title">Production over prototypes</div>
          <p class="philosophy-card__text">
            High-performing models are not products. Systems are products.
            They must tolerate imperfect data, fail visibly,
            support iteration without destabilization, and remain interpretable.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="philosophy-card">
          <div class="philosophy-card__num">02</div>
          <div class="philosophy-card__title">Explicit constraints</div>
          <p class="philosophy-card__text">
            Latency vs. accuracy. Automation vs. quality control.
            Throughput vs. cost. Scalability vs. interpretability.
            Trade-offs are engineered deliberately rather than deferred.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="philosophy-card">
          <div class="philosophy-card__num">03</div>
          <div class="philosophy-card__title">Research to deployment</div>
          <p class="philosophy-card__text">
            Academic results are starting points, not endpoints.
            Bridging to production requires clarifying assumptions,
            identifying failure modes, and designing operational feedback loops.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="philosophy-card">
          <div class="philosophy-card__num">04</div>
          <div class="philosophy-card__title">Data-centric AI</div>
          <p class="philosophy-card__text">
            Long-term system advantage emerges from data quality, not model novelty.
            Structured ingestion, annotation pipelines, automated QC,
            retraining triggers, and rollback strategies.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── Systems & Capabilities ─── -->
    <section id="systems">
      <h2>Systems & Capabilities</h2>

      <div class="card-grid card-grid--2">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__label">Pipelines</div>
          <div class="card__title">End-to-End Geospatial</div>
          <p class="card__text">
            Raw data ingestion, spatial processing and normalization,
            analytics and inference, quality control and validation,
            reporting and delivery. Designed for repeatability,
            auditability, and scale.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__label">Sensing</div>
          <div class="card__title">Multimodal Remote Sensing</div>
          <p class="card__text">
            Workflows across RGB imagery, thermal and infrared data,
            and derived spatial layers. Focus on extracting actionable
            signals while controlling false positives and uncertainty.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__label">Quality</div>
          <div class="card__title">Verification & QC</div>
          <p class="card__text">
            Spatial data often fails silently. QC is a first-class
            system component: automated checks, spatial sanity validation,
            human-in-the-loop review, reproducible metrics.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__label">Delivery</div>
          <div class="card__title">Secure Data Delivery</div>
          <p class="card__text">
            Multi-tenant access control, lifecycle and retention policies,
            auditability and permission boundaries. Architectures designed
            for operational trust.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── Research ─── -->
    <section id="research">
      <h2>Research & Scholarly Work</h2>
      <p>
        Academic work focuses on remote sensing and geospatial analysis,
        with peer-reviewed publications in journals and conferences.
        Research contributes methods and insights in GIS and spatial
        analytics, LiDAR and 3D data processing, and remote sensing
        methodologies.
      </p>

      <div style="margin-top: 1.75rem;">
        <div class="kv-item__key">Domains</div>
        <ul class="inline-list" style="margin-top: 0.65rem;">
          <li>GIS & Spatial Analytics</li>
          <li>LiDAR & 3D Processing</li>
          <li>Remote Sensing</li>
          <li>Geospatial AI</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="links-row" style="margin-top: 1.75rem;">
        <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=TcDAyj0AAAAJ&hl=en"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Scholar</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── Engineering (Abstracted) ─── -->
    <section id="engineering">
      <h2>Selected Engineering Work</h2>
      <blockquote>
        Descriptions are intentionally generalized and omit sensitive or
        proprietary information.
      </blockquote>

      <div class="subsection">
        <h3 class="subsection__title">Large-Scale Imagery Processing Systems</h3>
        <ul class="subsection__list">
          <li>Automated processing of high-resolution spatial data</li>
          <li>Built-in verification and QC layers</li>
          <li>Emphasis on repeatability and operational robustness</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="subsection">
        <h3 class="subsection__title">Multisensor Analysis Workflows</h3>
        <ul class="subsection__list">
          <li>Integration of RGB, thermal, and derived spatial data</li>
          <li>Signal extraction under uncertainty and operational constraints</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="subsection">
        <h3 class="subsection__title">Secure Delivery Architectures</h3>
        <ul class="subsection__list">
          <li>Multi-tenant delivery patterns</li>
          <li>Strict access control and lifecycle management</li>
          <li>Audit-friendly system design</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── Contact ─── -->
    <section id="contact">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <ul class="contact-list">
        <li>
          <a href="mailto:nan.shang@droneinstitute.ai">nan.shang@droneinstitute.ai</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="mailto:sn1514826@gmail.com">sn1514826@gmail.com</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <div class="links-row">
        <a href="https://github.com/leibowivz" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=TcDAyj0AAAAJ&hl=en"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Scholar</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <!-- ─── Footer ─── -->
    <footer>
      <p>Dr. Nan Shang — Built with Astro</p>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Base>
